title: EndRound3
position: 110,-41
---
<<notmove Cat>>
<<wait  2>>
Steve: Well, here we go again.
Clark: We really need to automate corpse disposal.
<<wait  1>>
Clark: You know, it's crazy to think that a cat could survive this.
Steve: What do you mean?
Clark: I mean, a cat can survive <color=green>1</color> exposure. It's the <color=red>2nd</color> one that seals the deal actually.
Steve: Really!?
Clark: Yeah. Are you deaf? I'm telling you. Any of these cats can survive with a <color=green>single dose</color> in their lungs. The only problem is that they would need medical attention for the rest of their life.
Steve: So, that means that anything after the <color=red>2nd</color> exposure is like beating a dead horse.
Clark: Well, yes.
<<if !$eatenFish>>
    Steve: Wait, I feel like something is missing.
    <<jump HasFoundFishBefore>>
<<endif>>
<<move Cat>>
===

title: EndRound4
